# R session and editor state
.Rproj.user
*.Rproj
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Renviron
.Rapp.history

# Credentials and local configuration. None of these has ever been in this
# repository; they are listed so that a stray one cannot be added by `git add -A`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
.httr-oauth
**/settings.local.json

# Build and check artefacts
inst/doc
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck/
..Rcheck/
src/*.o
src/*.so
src/*.dll

# The rendered pkgdown site. Rebuilt from the sources by the pkgdown workflow
# and published to the gh-pages branch; a copy on main would go stale the moment
# a vignette changed. NOT to be confused with pkgdown/, which holds the favicon
# and IS tracked.
docs/

# Run outputs. Any directory a run writes into, whatever it is called.
results/
results_*/
*_results/

# Demonstration cohort from the README quick start: FCS written from the GvHD
# dataset that ships with flowCore, together with its sample sheet and panel.
# Regenerated by inst/scripts/demo_data.R, and third-party data does not belong
# in the history.
demo/

# Benchmark scratch: downloaded public data, tool outputs, timings. Never
# tracked -- it is regenerated by benchmark/benchmark.R and would otherwise
# put hundreds of MB of third-party FCS into the history.
benchmark/

# Maintainer working files: backlog, release procedure, draft commit messages.
# See dev/README.md. Local to a working copy, never part of the package or the
# history.
dev/

# Patient data must never enter this repository. The analyses this package was
# written for keep their FCS files, sample sheets and results OUTSIDE the
# checkout, which is the actual safeguard; these patterns are a second line of
# defence against a stray copy, not a substitute for that separation.
*.fcs
*.fcs\ copy
data/
data_*/
*_cohort*/
patient_table*.csv
!inst/examples/patient_table_template.csv

# Operating system and editor droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
